window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-942299c0d854feb0"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"prepare-meeting-briefs\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">准备会议简报</h1> <p>根据日历背景整理会议议程和记录计划。</p> <p>使用 ChatGPT 配合 Calendar、Drive、Slack 和 Gmail，在会议前从获准的来源收集信息，然后起草会议目标、议程、问题和记录模板。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>会议背景分散在日历邀请、文档、Slack 讨论串、邮件和笔记中的情况。</li> <li>希望获得有来源依据的会前材料包的经理、产品团队、运营人员和面试官。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-calendar（需联网）</a></td> <td>查找会议、参会人、时间，以及应该影响简报的相关资料。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>阅读已关联的文档、访谈记录、预读材料、跟踪表和来源文件。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果会议依赖 Slack 中的内容，查找最新的计划讨论、决策背景或协作者更新。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail（需联网）</a></td> <td>检查相关邮件会话中的日程变更、附件或外部背景。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>整理会前简报</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>low</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">帮我准备 [meeting] 在 [date] 举行的会议。\n\n只使用以下来源：\n- 日历事件：[event name or date range]\n- 文档或笔记：[links or names]\n- Slack 频道或讨论串：[optional]\n- Gmail 邮件会话或发件人：[optional]\n\n请先盘点你能够访问的来源，并指出缺失的来源。\n\n请返回：\n- 会议目标\n- 参会人背景\n- 有来源依据的关键事实\n- 可能的议程\n- 尚待回答的问题\n- 我可能需要承担的决策或后续事项\n- 可在会议中填写的记录模板\n\n将缺少来源支持的说法放在单独的“来源缺口”部分。未经我批准，不要更新文档、发送消息或分享简报。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">将 ChatGPT 与 Google Calendar 搭配使用</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT 桌面应用</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"prepare-from-the-sources-you-already-have\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">从现有资料着手准备</h2> <p>会议背景往往不只在日历邀请中：预读材料可能放在 Drive，决策可能记录在 Slack，邮件会话里可能有相关信息，也可能需要回看之前的会议记录。</p> <p>可以让 ChatGPT 汇总获准使用的资料，并起草一份简短的会前简报，其中包含目标、议程、尚待回答的问题和记录模板。</p> <p><a id=\"gather-the-right-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">收集合适的背景信息</h2> <ol> <li>说明会议名称、日期或日历事件。</li> <li>指定 ChatGPT 可以使用的文档、笔记、Slack 讨论串、邮件会话或文件夹。</li> <li>先要求 ChatGPT 盘点来源，再开始撰写简报。</li> <li>要求它区分已确认的背景、来源缺口和待回答的问题。</li> <li>如果需要记录会议决策，可请它提供记录模板或评分表。</li> </ol> <p>如果是面试流程，可以让 ChatGPT 阅读获准使用的面试记录或问题库，再生成结构化评分表。对于周期性规划会议，可以要求它对照上次记录与最新资料更新，让议程聚焦于发生了哪些变化。</p> <p><a id=\"keep-the-brief-scannable\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">让简报便于快速浏览</h2> <p>只要求对你有帮助的必要内容。简报可以采用类似下面的格式：</p> <p><strong>目标：</strong> 判断未来两周的上线计划是否有足够的负责人覆盖。</p> <p><strong>背景：</strong> 预读材料里有一份负责人分工草稿，但 Slack 中两项后续事项还没有确定日期。</p> <p><strong>问题：</strong> 谁负责合作方审核？公开文案的最终锁定日期是什么？</p> <p><strong>会议记录模板：</strong> 决策、负责人、日期、风险和后续事项。</p> <p>如果简报包含私人或敏感信息，请将输出留在当前聊天中，并让 ChatGPT 标出哪些内容不适合放进共享文档。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this prep brief into a live notes template.\n\nKeep the source-backed context short, then add sections for:\n\n- decisions\n- owners and dates\n- risks\n- unanswered questions\n- follow-ups I owe\n- follow-ups other people own\n\nFlag anything private that doesn't belong in a shared meeting doc.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请将这份会前准备简报整理成现场记录模板。\n\n简短保留有来源支持的背景，然后添加以下章节：\n\n- 决策\n- 负责人和日期\n- 风险\n- 未回答的问题\n- 我需要跟进的事项\n- 由其他人负责跟进的事项\n\n标出任何不适合放在共享会议文档中的私密内容。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"prepare-meeting-briefs\">Prepare meeting briefs</h1> <p>Turn calendar context into an agenda and notes plan.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with Calendar, Drive, Slack, and Gmail to gather approved sources before a meeting, then draft objectives, agenda, questions, and a notes template.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Meetings where context is split across calendar invites, docs, Slack threads, email, and notes.</li> <li>Managers, product teams, operators, and interviewers who want a source-backed prep packet.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-calendar\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-calendar (online)</a></td> <td>Find the meeting, attendees, timing, and attached material that should shape the brief.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read linked docs, interview notes, pre-reads, trackers, and source artifacts.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Pull the latest planning thread, decision context, or collaborator updates when the meeting depends on them.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/gmail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">gmail (online)</a></td> <td>Check related email threads for scheduling changes, attachments, or external context.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build the Prep Brief</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>low</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Help me prepare for [meeting] on [date].\n\nUse only these sources:\n- calendar event: [event name or date range]\n- docs or notes: [links or names]\n- Slack channels or threads: [optional]\n- Gmail thread or sender: [optional]\n\nFirst, inventory the sources you can access and name any source gaps.\n\nReturn:\n- meeting objective\n- attendee context\n- key source-backed facts\n- likely agenda\n- open questions\n- decisions or follow-ups I may owe\n- suggested notes template for the meeting\n\nKeep unsupported claims in a separate source gaps section. Do not update docs, send messages, or share the brief until I approve it.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Use ChatGPT with Google Calendar</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">ChatGPT desktop app</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"prepare-from-the-sources-you-already-have\">Prepare from the sources you already have</h2> <p>Meeting context often lives outside the calendar invite. There may be a pre-read in Drive, a decision in Slack, an email thread, or notes from an earlier conversation.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT to gather the approved sources and draft a short prep brief with the objective, agenda, open questions, and a notes template.</p> <h2 id=\"gather-the-right-context\">Gather the right context</h2> <ol> <li>Name the meeting, date, or calendar event.</li> <li>Point ChatGPT at the docs, notes, Slack threads, email threads, or folders it can use.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to inventory the sources before writing the brief.</li> <li>Have it separate confirmed context, source gaps, and open questions.</li> <li>Ask for a notes template or scorecard if you need to capture decisions during the meeting.</li> </ol> <p>For interview loops, ask ChatGPT to read the approved notes or question bank, then produce a structured scorecard. For recurring planning meetings, ask it to compare the last notes with the latest source updates so the agenda starts from what changed.</p> <h2 id=\"keep-the-brief-scannable\">Keep the brief scannable</h2> <p>Ask for the smallest output that will help. You should get something like this:</p> <p><strong>Objective:</strong> decide whether the launch plan has enough owner coverage for the next two weeks.</p> <pre><code>**Context:** the pre-read has a draft owner map, but two\nfollow-up items in Slack still need dates.\n\n\n\n\n**Questions:** who owns partner review, and what is the latest\ndate for the public copy freeze?\n\n\n\n\n**Notes template:** decisions, owners, dates, risks, and\nfollow-ups.\n</code></pre> <p>If the brief includes private or sensitive information, keep the output local to the chat and ask ChatGPT to flag anything that doesn't belong in a shared doc.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Turn this prep brief into a live notes template.\n\nKeep the source-backed context short, then add sections for:\n\n- decisions\n- owners and dates\n- risks\n- unanswered questions\n- follow-ups I owe\n- follow-ups other people own\n\nFlag anything private that doesn't belong in a shared meeting doc.\n</code></pre>"};
